Miniaturized Day-Date Mechanism: Compact planetary gear systems reducing automatic movement thickness.
In-House Caliber 46 Series (1971): One of the most rugged, high-volume mechanical tractor movements ever produced, exceeding 100 million units.
Curatorial Narrative:
While Swiss watchmakers consolidated into luxury conglomerates and Japanese peers pivoted heavily toward quartz, Orient maintained an uninterrupted tradition of in-house mechanical watchmaking for everyday citizens. The Fineness proved that Japanese mechanical miniaturization could beat Swiss ultra-thin records, while the Multi-Year Calendar created an iconic, instantly recognizable dial architecture.
Unique UI/UX Interaction Component (Orient-Inspired):
The Multi-Year Calendar Disc Wheel: An interactive multi-disc calculator allowing users to rotate the calendar crown to match any historical year between 1976 and 2050, instantly aligning the calendar day and date matrices.
Visual Direction & Imagery Cues (Extracted from Orient-watch.com):
