7. Technical Performance, Rendering & Asset Guidelines
Asset Compression & Delivery Protocol:
WebGL Models: Compressed using Draco geometry compression and KTX2 texture basis format to ensure total model payloads stay under $3.5\text{ MB}$ per timepiece.
Macro Visuals: Shot in native $8\text{K}$ resolution, delivered dynamically via modern image CDNs in AVIF and WebP formats with progressive blur-up rendering.
Rendering Performance Benchmarks:
Maintain strict $60\text{ fps}$ animations on desktop and $60\text{ fps}$ on mobile during Three.js canvas rotations and loupe magnification tracking.
First Contentful Paint (FCP) $\le 0.8\text{ seconds}$.
Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) =0.
Accessibility & Semantic Architecture:
All interactive WebGL canvases must feature semantic HTML table fallbacks for screen readers, exposing all caliber specifications, historical notes, and dimension matrices.
Full contrast compliance ($\text{WCAG AAA}$) for all typography set against the Imperial Purple, Royal Navy, and Obsidian backgrounds.

